      "Traveler's diarrhea affects a large share of visitors to lower-income destinations; the graded expert guideline and systematic reviews cover what prevents it — food and water choices, and in selected travellers chemoprophylaxis with a non-absorbed antibiotic or a probiotic yeast, both described here rather than advised. Heat-related illness research from the Hajj and from desert expeditions shows the pattern of who gets sick and when, and a systematic review found that interventions promoting sun-protective behaviour in recreational and tourist settings can work. The routine is unglamorous and daily, which is why it is fundamental.",
